# WU/W9: the remaining routes and small flows in the real app, against the showcase scenario.
# The server is asked for what it hasn't been set up as yet, what it says about registering, an
# invite to a community alexk isn't in (joined with his account, and one he can't use), the
# notifications page (all read), the friends, profile and create-community routes, a channel's
# search route with a page of results and the next one, a group DM's "Add people" and "Leave
# group", the web's shortcuts: Ctrl+/ for the sheet, Escape to close it, Alt+Down for the next
# channel, and About from the account menu: the version this build reports, and Escape closes it.
# Then Escape in a conversation, one thing per press: the side panel closes, and with the list
# detached from the live edge the conversation is marked read.
#
# Two windows: the signed-out screens at the size the other lanes use, then (signed out, so no
# session is lost) a tall one, because the search panel's "More results" sits below fifty hits
# and a click needs it in the window. The rig can only open a window, not resize one.
app 1600 1400
window activate
wait idle

# 1. A server nobody has set up yet: the connect screen says to set it up in a browser, and its
# button opens that page.
server onboarding "{\"needsSetup\": true}"
click auth-connect
# The probe announces `ViewChanged { Session }` itself when its answer changes, so the screen
# says the server needs setting up at once: no other core event provokes it, and the sign-in
# form never shows.
wait core w9 setup-notice shown
wait idle
shot 01-setup-notice
click auth-setup-open
expect opened-url "$SERVER"
# Set up in the browser now: back to the connect step, and the probe says so.
click auth-setup-change-server
wait core element auth-connect
server onboarding "{\"needsSetup\": false}"
click auth-connect
wait core w9 setup-notice gone
wait core label "Username"

# 2. Registering: closed (not offered), invite-only (the code required), open (optional).
server public_settings "{\"registrationMode\": \"CLOSED\"}"
click auth-change-server
wait core element auth-connect
click auth-connect
wait core element auth-register-closed
wait core no-element auth-register
wait idle
shot 02-register-closed
server public_settings "{\"registrationMode\": \"INVITE_ONLY\"}"
click auth-change-server
wait core element auth-connect
click auth-connect
wait core element auth-register
click auth-register
wait core element register-code
wait core label "Invite code"
wait idle
shot 03-register-invite-only
click register-sign-in
server public_settings "{\"registrationMode\": \"OPEN\"}"
click auth-change-server
wait core element auth-connect
click auth-connect
wait core element auth-register
click auth-register
wait core element register-code
wait core label "Invite code (optional)"
wait idle
shot 04-register-open
click register-sign-in

# The tall window: nothing is signed in yet, so no session is left behind by the one this
# replaces.
app 1600 3600
window activate
wait idle
click auth-connect
wait core label "Username"
click auth-username
type "alexk"
click auth-password
type "hunter2"
click auth-login
wait core session signed-in
wait core connection connected
wait idle

# 3. The notifications page: the showcase's unread ones, then every one read.
navigate /notifications
wait core route /notifications
wait core element notifications-page
# "Mark all as read" is offered exactly while something is unread.
wait core element notifications-mark-all
wait idle
shot 05-notifications
click notifications-mark-all
wait core w9 unread-notifications 0
wait core no-element notifications-mark-all
wait idle
shot 06-notifications-read

# 4. The friends page, his profile by `/profile`, and the create-community route.
navigate /friends
wait core route /friends
wait core element friends-panel
wait idle
shot 07-friends
navigate /profile
wait core route profile/$ID(me)
wait core element profile-edit
wait idle
shot 08-profile
navigate /community/create
wait core element create-community-name
wait idle
shot 09-create-community
click create-community-cancel
wait core no-element create-community-name

# 5. A channel's search route: more hits than one page holds, so the panel offers the next page,
# and takes it.
navigate /community/$ID(c-couch)/channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"w9needle 1\"}"
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"w9needle 2\"}"
server post_as "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"authorId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"text\": \"w9needle 3\"}"
